WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
The paper makes three main contributions.

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:06.680
First,

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:10.060
it reviews existing privacy-preserving machine
learning approaches to expose their limitations

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.440
and the room for improvement.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.820
Second, it proposes a concrete framework in which
each peer trains an autoencoder,

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:20.200
shares only the latent-space representation of its data,

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:23.580
and then joins these embeddings to train a shared
supervised model.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.960
Third,

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:30.340
it validates the framework on three public datasets
spanning regression and classification,

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.720
and across five experimental scenarios,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.100
ranging from a raw-data baseline to non-naive
multitask autoencoders that also predict

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:40.480
the target variable during encoding.
